cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use the Universal Trust Model (UTM) in your research, software,
  or teaching material, please cite this work using the metadata below.
title: Universal Trust Model (UTM)
date-released: 2025-06-29

authors:
  - family-names: Carlisle
    given-names: Ryan

abstract: >
  The Universal Trust Model (UTM) is a parameterised learning framework for
  modelling trust dynamics in repeated decision scenarios. It generalises
  reinforcement-style updates via theta (θ), positive and negative learning
  rates (α⁺, α⁻), a cumulative update ramp (δ), and a behavioural threshold (τ).

repository-code: https://github.com/ignitum-solutions/utm-ipd
url: https://utm.ignitumsolutions.com
license: MIT

